---
import NarrativePage from '../components/NarrativePage.astro'
const page = {
  "title": "Veqtor Workspace — Local files and data handling",
  "description": "Understand the boundary between local document work, your AI conversation, working copies and file saving in Veqtor Workspace.",
  "eyebrow": "Security and privacy",
  "heading": "Local files. A connected AI assistant.",
  "lede": "Veqtor works on your Mac. Document content returned to the assistant becomes part of your AI conversation and may be processed by its provider.",
  "sections": [
    {
      "id": "local",
      "title": "What stays on your Mac",
      "body": [
        "Veqtor keeps the source file, task snapshot, working copy and local logs on your Mac. The website does not receive your working documents. Stored copies and logs may contain document text; there is no automatic cleanup."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "provider",
      "title": "What the assistant receives",
      "body": [
        "The assistant can receive text and other information read from the selected documents. Its provider processes that conversation under your account’s terms and settings. Working with local files does not make the assistant offline."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "access",
      "title": "How document access works",
      "body": [
        "The assistant selects file and folder paths based on your instructions. The local process that runs document-editing code can read the paths granted for that task, write inside its working area and has no network access. Those restrictions apply to that process, not to every other tool available to the assistant."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "saving",
      "title": "What the save check protects",
      "body": [
        "Veqtor edits a private copy. Before replacing the selected original, it checks whether the on-disk file changed since the task began. A new filename creates a separate file and does not overwrite an existing destination.",
        "Unsaved Word edits are not visible to this check. Save first, avoid simultaneous edits, and reopen the document after the assistant updates it."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "review",
      "title": "Review remains part of the workflow",
      "body": [
        "Optional document checks can report possible unexpected changes. They are not a guarantee of correctness, complete compatibility or a check of the file in Microsoft Word."
      ]
    }
  ],
  "path": "/security",
  "linkSection": {
    "eyebrow": "Related",
    "title": "More about working with documents",
    "links": [
      {
        "href": "/privacy",
        "title": "Privacy"
      },
      {
        "href": "/limitations",
        "title": "Current limitations"
      },
      {
        "href": "/docs",
        "title": "Technical documentation"
      },
      {
        "href": "/how-it-works",
        "title": "How it works"
      }
    ]
  }
}
---
<NarrativePage {...page} />
